I finally fixed this problem - and would classify this as a user error.

I ftp'd the samba-2.0.7-21ssl.src.rpm and used rpm --rebuild to rebuild the
entire the rpm (with ssl). I had to ftp openssl-devel rpm as well for this.
Upon installation of the 3 newly built rpm's, and enabling swat (changes
include localhost to 127.0.0.1 , and disable = no), and configuring smb
(/sbin/chkconfig -level 5 smb on) - I have been able to mount my linux
shares on windows 98SE.

Mohan




