Recompile may not fix it...

Alpha is a RISC machine and expects all the data it processes to be on word
boundary's.

When Data is accessed which is not on a word boundary, (a piece of byte data
in a structure), it performs a trap, and processes the data using firmware
emulation of byte instructions, to let the programmer know what is going on,
a informational/warning  message is printed to the console device "unaligned
trap".  This is not an error, but simply letting you know the program is
wasting time executing emulated byte instructions, and yes, newer CPU's have
the byte instructions but they still waste time and the messages are still
generated.

If you do a search on the redhat axp-list  mailing list, the procedure for
identifying the piece of code causing the trap is explained in some of the
message threads.

JJ

