Jim Dennis (jimd@vega.starshine.org) wrote:

:  Any suggestions?

I've had luck opening those cylindrical locks using a paperclip and a
small screwdriver.

Take a paperclip and bend the end of it into a circle that will fit into
the circular keyhole.  Press it all the way into the keyhole without 
breaking it off in the lock.  Insert the tip of a small flathead
screwdriver into the notched part of the keyhole.  With a bit of adjusting
you should be able to turn the lock pretty easily.

Good luck.
