For RH 7.0, I suggest the following boot command:
(Insert the CD)
b dka4 -fi kernels/vmlinux.gz -fl "initrd=/images/ramdisk.img 
console=ttyS0,9600 serial expert text"

Of course, you'll have to think about change the device dka4, and also 
throw away any other options that you don't want.  Typical user will do:
b dka4 -fi kernels/vmlinux.gz -fl initrd=/images/ramdisk.img


