Try putting loadlin and milo on the same (DOS-formatted) disk.
Put udb-noname.gz on a separate disk.
> 
> I set up the entries in the boot selection menu correctly, afaik.
> 
LoadIdentifier=Linux Floppy                  ***optional
> systempartition was multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
> osloader was multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)\linload.exe
> osloadpartition was multi(0)disk(0)fdisk(0)
> osloadfilename was \udb-noname
try osloadfilename \MILO      (or whatever your MILO filename is)
> no osloadoptions
try osloadoptions boot fd0:udb-noname.gz load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1

The loader (linload) has to load MILO, which sets up the system,
then loads and runs the kernel. You need to set osloadoptions to the
MILO commands to load and start the kernel.

