Mohan Vaghul <mohan.vaghul@gte.net> wrote:

> I just installed RH 7.0 on my alpha, and am wondering if there are any
> documents associated with the upgrade.

Well, yes, there are. "Release Notes", for example, and there is
a whole CD with documentation for 7.0 (this stuff will be the same
regardless of architecture).

> I find that the inetd.conf file is no
> longer present in the /etc/ directory and am not sure how the samba
> process
> (swat) gets started.

inetd was replaced by xinetd. See /usr/share/doc/xinetd-*/*,
'man xinetd', 'man xinetd.conf', 'man xinetd.log' and possibly also
/usr/sbin/inetdconvert (it is written in Python so enthusiast of
this language will tell you that its code should be obvious to
everybody :-).  'xinetd' works on the same principle as 'inetd'
although some configuration details are slightly different.

> If any body has installed samba on RH 7.0, I would appreciate any
> pointers to docs or tips.

'chkconfig --list' shows swat as one of xinetd based services which
is off by default.  Typing 'locate swat' reveals not only an existence
of /etc/xinetd.d/swat but also of the whole book, 416 pages, in 
/usr/share/swat/using_samba/ on the top of some 2.5 MB of documentation
in /usr/share/doc/samba*/ (although it beats me why "Using Samba"
resides in /usr/share/swat/ :-).

   Michal


