Hello,

we have some problems with our new ES40 Alpha server.

Machine configuration:
4x 667Mhz EV67 cpus
8 GByte RAM (which seems to have ECC errors)
Powerstorm 350D video adapter
Intel 82557 EtherExpressPro network adapter
NCR 53c895 SCSI controller

I've tried the standard SuSE7 2.2.16 kernel and a self compiled
2.4.0 kernel from ftp.kernel.org (with gcc 2.91.66).

The 2.2.16 kernel seems to work stable besides the network adapter
under heavy load. In the log file appers following message and the
connection hangs for about 2 seconds:

Jan 22 13:32:23 beta kernel: eth0: Transmit timed out: status 0050  
0c00 at 504012/504040 command 000c0000.
Jan 22 13:32:23 beta kernel: eth0: Tx ring dump,  Tx queue 504040 / 504012:
Jan 22 13:32:23 beta kernel: eth0:     0 200ca000.
Jan 22 13:32:23 beta kernel: eth0:     1 000ca000.
....
Jan 22 13:32:38 beta kernel: eth0: Printing Rx ring (next to receive into 304899, dirty index 304899).
....

After this period, the network transfer goes on. Further the 2.2.16 kernel
doensn't recognize all of the CPUs and memory.

Question: Is there a solution for this network problem?


The 2.4.0 kernel has the same network problem and it works unstable.
From time to time the kernel freezes the complete machine and I have to
power off/on to resurrect the machine. 

In the logs of the 2.2.16 kernel I've seen several messages concerning
ECC memory errors. 

Question: It is possible that the reason for the system crashes of the
2.4.0 kernel is the ECC memory problem, or it is possible, to compile
such a ECC detection in the 2.4.0 kernel?


Thanks a lot!


Bye,
Christian


