>Im trying to install Linux on an Alpha 2100A, it
>has aboot version 0.5 and SRM version V5.3-14.

During the install, it makes no difference what aboot you have already
installed.  aboot is a program that resides in the boot sector of the
hard disk (or other disk) and it has the ability to search through an
ext2 fs, find the kernel, and transfer program execution. When you boot
from CD, the aboot on your hd is completely ignored; the aboot on the
boot sector of the CD is used instead. 

