RL Griswold <rgriswol@us.ibm.com> writes:

> Where can I find information on running DU binaries on Alpha Linux?  I
> know it's possible, since that's how I run Netscape at home.  What I
> need is inforamation on how its done (intercepting syscalls, emulation,
> etc).

It's just intercepting syscalls and a special binary loader. Alpha
Linux was designed from the start to support OSF, so it wasn't that
hard. Look in linux/arch/alpha/kernel/entry.S: OSF syscalls have IDs
below 300, the linux specific start above that. Some of the weirder
OSF syscalls get special treatment in
linux/arch/alpha/kernel/osf_sys.c.

> Also, does the opposite work as well (Alpha Linux binaries on DU)?

No. It might not even be possible, since some Linux syscalls like
clone() might not be implementable, though that seems unlikely.

	Falk



