I don't have a PWS, but there is some info in the VMS FAQ about SRM booting
from the IDE CDROM drive (specifically for OpenVMS, but it might be the 
same issue).  

OpenVMS will only boot from the IDE CDROM on PWS systems built with the
Cypress IDE controller, not the Intel Saturn SIO chip.  If the system
has the Saturn chip then VMS (which uses SRM console exclusively) requires
a SCSI CDROM to boot.  Maybe its actually an SRM limitation?

If you do a 'show config' at the prompt it will tell you if you have
"Cypress PCI Peripheral Controller" or "Intel SIO 82378" in your PWS.

Shot in the dark...

Rich Jordan

