I've never used your particular board but I
did have to mess with the evaluation board
SRM stuff for an EB64 and Takara some time ago.

None of the stuff above looks like an error to me.
It's letting you know what its doing.
In particular it seems to be booting a debug srm.
This might be to do with however you have the
jumpers set or it might be perfectly
normal.

You don't say exactly what you are trying to
do with the IDE that is causing you trouble.

Back in the EB64/Takara days, the SRM would
not boot from an IDE device ... it just
would not see them. It knew about SCSI.

The ARC console (now replaced by the
AlphaBIOS) could happily boot WNT
from an IDE device so this was clearly
just an SRM issue.

Since that time some Alphas have acquired
IDE support. This one looks too old for
that to work.

Or it could be that having entered the debug
monitor (for whatever reason) you now
need to get the SRM console running.

I don't know how to do that. Pretty
much all the manuals for evaluation machines
of that era *were* available on the
digital ftp site. I have not looked
lately so I don't know if they are still 
there.

If you cannot find them, send me email
(in case I miss your followup) and I'll
see if I saved one.

Antonio

