>Which distribution should I install on a digital alpha 255. I'm a linux
>begginner...

As a linux beginner, it doesn't make too much difference which distribution 
you use, as long as you can successfully get it installed, have a decent 
selection of software, GUI, and have a decent learning experience out of 
it.

An incomplete list of popular distributions is:
Debian, Turbolinux, RedHat, SuSE, Storm (aka Stormix), and Mandrake.
AFAIK, Stormix isn't available on alpha.

IMO, you will get the best learning experience by having at least several-
gigs of hard drive, and install a selection of distributions onto different 
partitions.  Choose which one you'll boot each bootup, and you'll get the 
best feel for what things are different from one distro to the next.

Of that list, you'd do pretty well with:
Red Hat, SuSE, or Mandrake.
Debian and Turbolinux aren't quite as user-friendly.
Red Hat is common for beginners, but I don't know why.  I always found it 
to be somewhat prone to breaking.
SuSE has the largest set of bells and whistles (it comes on 6 CDs, and 
therefore is hard to find iso images on the net).  SuSE is my favorite.
Mandrake is a modified version of Red Hat.  Some like the modifications, 
and others don't.

The most important thing, though, is:
Which one(s) will work on your machine?
I don't know the answer to that question.


