Unfortunately, the early PWS boxes support a very limited set of graphics
cards. The FreeBSD hardware compatibility discussion points out that the
early PWS boxes have a hardware design flaw that restricts the block
transfer mechanism. The way the SRM deals with this is to limit the box to
known cards so the problem can be handled gracefully. It also mentions an
override that will allow the box to accept any card on an 'at your own risk'
basis, but I haven't tried it. The design flaw was apparently fixed in the
later generation PWS that has the Cypress IDE controller. Mine doesn't.

I bought an official (read pricey) DEC ati based card & the PWS SRM
indicates it is unsupported. Don't know of any Ati based cards that work in
the PWS. Maybe someone can point one out that they _know_ works. (vendor
wouldn't take it back as I had special ordered it... bummer.)

The Matrox cards work fine though, Millenum I, II, G200 etc apparently all
work. I use a Millenium I. Linux & the Matrox cards get along fine.

Return the card if you can. Or try the override.

EM

