Hi there... thought I might give you some advice.
what you might need to do is make the disk "bootable".
Here's an example how to go about doing this:

1. boot from floppy using  the command: boot dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags
"root=/dev/hda2" (change root path according to where your / partition is)

2. cd to where aboot.conf file is. Usually in /etc and type more aboot.conf.
Note the last line should be something like 0:2/boot/vmlinuz-2.2.17-4
root=/dev/hda2

3.enter the command: swriteboot /dev/hda /boot/bootlx /boot/vmlinuz-2.2.17-4

4. Shutdown system

5. >>>set boot_file 0/vmlinuz-2.2.17-4
    >>>set boot_osflags root=/dev/hda2
    >>>set bootdef_dev dkc0


Hope this helps

