It sounds like you didn't use BSD disklabels.    Basically, MILO needs
FAT partitions and SRM needs BSD disklabels.

When you format hard disks for SRM, the first command you need to run in
fdisk is 'b.'  This will switch to BSD disklabels.  Now you can partition
the disk pretty much (partitions are labeled as letters) as normal.  Also,
be sure to leave some space at the beginning of the drive free for aboot.

There should be plenty of HOWTO's out there with more detail.  Check
www.alphalinux.org

Hope this helps,

/Bill

