little information for ya.
RH will install aboot for you.
When you run the boot command, you're not supposed to get the "bad block" 
or whatever message.
The easiest way for a beginner to deal with this is to use the Jumpstart 
CD.
Let the jumpstart CD make your partitions for you.  I have never done this 
myself, so I assume it lets you ignore all of the following:

Don't use the first cylinder in any of your partitions.  The first cyl 
stores the disklabel, and should not be overwritten.
With old versions of fdisk, you should not use the last cyl.  There was a 
bug, but it has been corrected.
You need to be sure you install a BSD disklabel.


