Here's the experiment I did:

I have an Alphastation 500/333 sitting here, with a built-in ethernet 
adapter (eth0, ewa0, tu0) which is not being used.  (Because it's only 10 
Mbit)
It has an add-on pci adapter too:  DEC 21143-pc  auto-sensing 10/100 full 
duplex.  (eth1, ewb0, tu1)  This is connected to a 100/fd network.

At SRM, verify the card is in auto-sense mode:
| >>> set ewb0_mode auto
| Change mode to auto negotiate
| 
| ewb0: link up : Negotiated  100BaseTX: full duplex
boot into linux.  Transfer a file (using ftp, 8.72 MB/s, 56232 k)
shutdown, boot into Tru64.  Note the various messages saying 100, and full 
duplex.  Transfer the same file from the same host, through ftp.  10019 
Kbytes/s
shutdown, at SRM change the mode:
| >>> set ewb0_mode twisted
| Change mode to Twisted Pair
boot into linux.  Transfer the file.  8.69 MB/s
boot into Tru64.  Note the messages saying 10BaseT half.  Transfer same as 
before, 746 Kbytes/sec

These results are reproducible.  I repeated the procedure twice.


