I am assuming that you have a 3 channel Mylex card for your hotswap config.
If you do not have a Mylex ( DAC960 for Alpha ) then all bets are off. Make
sure that when you run the RA200RCU in " ALPHABIOS " that controller
settings are set for recovery. Then, there is nothing for the software to
do. As far as it is concerned, it only sees what you've told the controller
to let it see. If you want to add a drive, you will have to bring down the
system and rerun RA200RCU. If this is not your configuration, and you are
using a third party RAID controller, this won't help you. If you have a
normal SCSI controller and you want to be able to hat swap drives, you are
taking your chances. The act of inserting or removing a drive in one of
these, causes SCSI Bus transitions, which can corrupt your data during the
transfer. If you stop all I/O on that bus before you remove or insert a
drive, you are safe. Do not expect any software to recognize the new drive
though. You will have to create the device drivers before you can do
anything with it.

