Try booting from the SRM prompt with boot dka400 (or what ever the CD device
is in "show dev") -fi <path to kernel file on cd> -fl "root=/dev/sda5
single"

example --
boot dka400 -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda5 single"

This should boot you into linux off the harddrive but using the kernel on
the CD. This will cause some problems with drivers which you may need to use
insmod to install them. Now you will be able to repair or correct any
problems. you will not have networking due to the single mode but you can
after installiong modules needed for the network change to runlevel 3 by
executing "init 3" from the command line. The rest is up to you.

Brian Walton

