Georges, your message is a little confusing.  It looks like you want to run 
the text install, but have trouble.  If true, try this:

I assume your boot command looks like this:
    	b dka0 -fl 0
This translates (through /etc/aboot.cfg) to
    	b dka0 -fi kernels/vmlinux.gz -fl "initrd=/images/ramdisk.img"
If these assumptions are correct, try adding some of the following option 
flags, especially "text":
"initrd=/images/ramdisk.img console=ttyS0,9600 serial expert text"

