Georges,

I just got three XP-1000s and have been trying to install RH7.0 on
them.  I encountered exactly the same problem you've described on two of
them.  On one machine, the boot went very smoothly: after I gave the SRM
boot command, "boot dqa0 -flags 0",  Linux booted from the CD-ROM and I
dived into the GUI install with no trouble.  On the remaining two
machines, however, the boot hung right after it had loaded the
compressed kernel and initrd.img and was preparing to boot.   I muddled
this over for a while and realized that the only difference between my
first XP-1000 and the other two was the PCI slot which I chose for the
ELSA gloria synergy card.  On the first, I put it into the first open
slot, but on the other two I installed it into a lower PCI slot.  I do
not know if there's something wrong with the lower part of the bus or if
the Alpha requires that one use the PCI slots in a particular order, but
as soon as I moved the video card up, the CD-ROM boot went smoothly.

My advice: open your alpha and see if you need to move your video card.

I hope this helps.

-Daniel

