Are you sure you counted right?

Alphastation 200 Error Beep Codes...
Beep Code Description 
1-1-4     The SROM code could not read the DROM(diagnostic read only 
memory) or flashRom headers, or there was a checksum failure. 

1-2-1     The DROM code detected a realtime clock(BQ3287) failure, or the 
realtime clock interrupt did not occur. 

1-2-4     The SROM code detected a hard failure (for example, a Bcache 
failure). 

1-3-3     The SROM code could not find 2-MB of good memory, or there was no 
memory available. 

3-2-1     The DROM code was unable to read the header of the flashROM, or 
the flashROM checksum failed. Therefore, the DROM code attempted to boot 
from the floppy. The attempt failed because of either: no floppy in drive 
or no Alpha AXP boot block on the floppy. 

2-2-3 or  
3-2-3     The DROM code was directed by the position of jumper J2 to load 
the floppy, but there was no floppy in the drive. 

3-2-4     The DROM code detected a failure with the keyboard or the mouse 
controller. 

3-3-1     The DROM code detected a hard failure. Refer to the LED's to find 
exact location of failure. 


