The easiest way for you to do this is:
1. Create a firmware update floppy using the NT/Alphabios process, you can
create this floppy on any windowsXX system.

2. power up your PWS500au to the SRM prompt  ">>>"

3. insert the firmware floppy you created using the NT/Alphabios
instructions.

4 On your system console type "arc"  at the SRM prompt followed by a
carriage return.
>>> arc

5. The system will start the AlphaBios console from SRM,  While it's
performing selftest, press the F2 key. A message should appear on the bottom
of the screen stating setup will be entered when selftest completes.

6. on the setup menu, select update cmos.

7. follow instructions, update SRM, AlphaBios and srom  (I believe there is
a selection for "all roms")

8. when done, "POWER CYCLE" the box, it will automatically return to SRM


JJ

